  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "subsection",
      "he": "",
      "en": "My Day Is Ending, but the New One Just Started—Time to Daven!"
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "In the morning, we awaken and begin our day by affirming our commitment to our mission (the Shema) and we make our requests (Shemoneh Esrei) for what we need spiritually and materially in order to fulfill our mission successfully. Now, we end our day and set the tone for the next day (since each day really begins the night before) by once again affirming our commitment to our mission (the Shema) and again putting in our requests for the spiritual and material things we need to be successful. Still, in our heart of hearts we know that we did not really use all that Hashem gave us (our talents, character traits, our neshamah, and spiritual gifts) in the best way possible. Therefore, we start by focusing on the fact that Hashem is והוא רחום יכפר עון—He is all-merciful and ready to give us another day and another chance! With that confidence, we can stand in front of Him and declare our readiness to try again to maximize our potential. That gives us the ability to once again ask Hashem for the things we need, even though we wasted some of them today!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "subsection",
      "he": "",
      "en": "Hashem Is Always Ready to Give Us Another Day and Another Chance!"
